(136, '/uploads/audio/1790761164952_b9a1c82c_EG10_UNIT_5.B_4__High_quality_.mp3', U&'Conversation 1:\000d\000aLeakhena: Channy, did you see my keys anywhere? I can''t find them!\000d\000aChanny: Wait a minute. Are these the keys you''re looking for?\000d\000aLeakhena: No honey. Those are my office keys. I''m looking for our house keys.\000d\000aChanny: Have you checked your bag mom?\000d\000aLeakhena: Yes, but I''ve only got my purse and phone in my bag. Can you please go and check in the kitchen for me in case I left them there?\000d\000aChanny: Sure. [pause for few seconds - for going to the kitchen]. Mom, your keys aren''t\000d\000ain the kitchen! Did you check the bathroom? Leakhena: Not yet. Let me go now. [pause for few seconds - for checking the bathroom).\000d\000aChanny, I''ve found my keys! You are right.. I left them near the bathroom sink when washed my hands.\000d\000a\000d\000aConversation 2:\000d\000aTim: Wow, Kosal I can see you''ve got a new camera!\000d\000aKosal: Oh no. It isn''t mine. This is my dad''s camera. I just borrowed it from him.\000d\000aTim: I see. It looks really cool! Why did you bring this camera here today?\000d\000aKosal: Because our coach said he wanted to take some photos during our practice today but his professional camera is broken. So I told him I could bring my dad''s camera for him to use.\000d\000a\000d\000aConversation 3:\000d\000aSeller: Hi. How can I help you?\000d\000aVicki: Oh hello. I''m looking for some umbrellas.\000d\000aIt''s raining season soon and I want to get some new umbrella for my children.\000d\000aSeller: Oh we have so many here. What about these umbrellas?\000d\000aVicki: I think they''re too big for their bags. Have you got anything smaller?\000d\000aSeller: Sure, wait for a moment please.\000d\000a[pause for few seconds) What about these?\000d\000aDo you like them? Their colors are very nice too\000d\000aVicki: Perfect! I''ll get two-one in blue and one in orange please.', 99, 3, 'Transcript 3: 5B,4L